{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact fixed-slot history head 865227314b6a1982ea924617b916b41c845dca1f on builder/fixed-slot-histories-20261104, tree 53caf406, for request fd0cec33 under promise 8d063742 and review request fc58d272. This approval covers the four paths at this head. It claims no signer authority, application journey or archive cause.\n\nScope. Main 7135dc39 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head adds two commits, and the commit-message check passes for both. The only source change is packages/scope/test/fixed-index.test.ts. No production source, card path or dependency changes. Source commit 410a9466 has tree ba93294d, the gate tree. Only the note and the two manifests change after it.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The oracle is independent. `scanCount` filters a literal array of items by state membership and `===` on the slot value. It calls no index, normalization, fold or `MemoryState` helper. After every command, the test compares the stored items with that array. It then checks 7 needles × 3 state sets × 2 modes against the scan.\n- The histories are legal and bounded. Four fixed orders × three value sets give 12 histories of 16 commands. Each history keeps four persistent items, including the legacy one. Every close and aborted close asserts that its target is still live. Every append asserts the next sequence.\n- Rollback and rebuild preserve state. Each aborted transaction asserts an unchanged `stateDigest`, and so does the clear-and-rebuild of the four fixed tables. The repeat commands write each fixed row twice through the real `fixedRowsOf` and `putFixed`.\n- The legacy gap is exercised as the request asks. Before the base-writer append, `fixedReady` is true for the current head. The append changes items and the scope head without fixed writes. The marker bytes stay unchanged, and the restart follows with no query in between. The next check must then rebuild for the new head and count the appended duplicate.\n- The existing witnesses